# Local secrets for `npm run worker:dev` (wrangler dev reads `.dev.vars`).
# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` (gitignored) and replace every value. Never commit real values.
#
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#
# The placeholders below are deliberately unusable: until you replace them, sign-in and Setup
# answer 503 "Server is not configured" instead of accepting a secret everybody can read here.
# The three values must be different from each other.

# The setup key: needed for the first-run Setup and for break-glass recovery of an admin. It is
# not anybody's sign-in password. At least 24 characters.
#   openssl rand -base64 24
APP_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME

# Key that signs the session cookie. At least 32 characters.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
JWT_SECRET=CHANGE_ME

# Protects what the server must read back (see docs/configuration.md). Base64 of exactly 32 random
# bytes. This placeholder is 32 zero bytes, which the Worker refuses on purpose.
#   openssl rand -base64 32
DATA_KEY=AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA=

# Optional: override the defaults from `vars` in wrangler.jsonc.
# APP_NAME="Edging Mail"
# DEFAULT_FROM=you@example.com

# Optional, local development only: also accept a Web Push endpoint on loopback over http or https (a fake
# push service). Without it only real push services over https are accepted. Never set it on a deployment.
# ALLOW_LOCAL_PUSH=on
